  <paragraphs xml:id="weekly-activities">
    <title>Daily Homework</title>
    <p>
      We will have daily pre-class assignments submitted via canvas prior to class each day. I will be grading these mainly on completion and effort. These assignments will be the foundation of our work in class each day. 
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="weekly-homework">
    <title>Weekly Homework</title>
    <p>
      Weekly written homework assignments will be assigned and graded for completeness, correctness, and presentation. I expect you to write these up formally, neatly, and completely (typeset with LaTex preferably) and submit them for more complete and rigorous feedback. 
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="midterm-exams">
    <title>Midterm Exams</title>
    <p>
      There will be four midterm exams given in class during weeks 4, 7, 10, and 13. 
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="project">
    <title>Project</title>
    <p>
       To round out the quarter, in groups of 2-3 we will investigate additional topics in topology (other than point set topology) and present them to the class. There will also be a written component for this project as well.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
  <paragraphs xml:id="final">
    <title>Cumulative Final Exam</title>
    <p>
      Your cumulative final exam will be Monday, April 27, from 9:45-11:45am.
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
</section>